('original:science--physical-science-chemistry--periodic-table-and-trends:science--physical-science-chemistry--periodic-table-and-trends--18',1,'{"question":"Across a period, atomic number rises by one at each step. What increases by one?","choices":["The number of isotopes in nature","The number of neutrons in every atom","The number of protons in the nucleus","The number of occupied shells"],"answer":2,"explanation":""}'::jsonb,'d3b935ebf410eaa16d323ac02611900a','official',NULL,NULL,'Periodic Table and Trends'),
