('original:science--physical-science-chemistry--chemical-bonding:science--physical-science-chemistry--chemical-bonding--10',1,'{"question":"Why are the bonds in an H₂ molecule nonpolar covalent?","choices":["The hydrogen atoms have different electronegativities","One atom gives its only proton to the other","The atoms do not share any electrons","Identical atoms attract the shared electrons equally"],"answer":3,"explanation":""}'::jsonb,'d660b9f7717395dc57f74090fb93d8cf','official',NULL,NULL,'Chemical Bonding'),
